  "semantics": [
    "Immutable strict CJSON records now validate/inspect root partialCharges as complete finite f64 arrays and properties.name as a string. Other properties and atoms.partialCharges remain opaque. Legacy graph-only parsing/writing remains unchanged.",
    "CJSON to MOL2 writes unrounded shortest decimal coordinates/partial charges and separately reparses name/method labels. Bitwise float preservation requires full projected graph correspondence.",
    "MOL2 metadata such as atom names/types/IDs is generated. Only +1 nitrogen via N.4 preserves a nonzero formal charge in this local adapter. Specified isotopes and unsupported formal charges are dropped, disable verified graph/mappings and remain explicit losses.",
    "Multiple datasets, invalid method/name representation, missing coordinates and empty molecules refuse even with allow_loss. Missing datasets emit NO_CHARGES without invented charge columns.",
    "Strict cross-format policy still refuses. No generic chemistry equivalence, stereo/typing completeness, published release or independent superiority claim."
  ]
}
